Vendored from crates.io spout2-sys 0.1.1 (BSD-2-Clause, Jaden Hills).
Includes Spout 2.007.017 (BSD-2-Clause, Lynn Jarvis).
Upstream source: https://docs.rs/crate/spout2-sys/0.1.1/source/
Changes: build.rs accepts MinGW-w64/CLANG64 as well as MSVC, enables
-fms-extensions where supported. Rust calls the flat C shim, not a C++ ABI.
See LICENSE and vendor/Spout2/LICENSE for the complete license notices.
MinGW/Clang portability changes in the bundled SDK:
- canonical GL/gl.h include casing (also permits cross compilation on Linux);
- SSSE3 target attributes on the four explicitly SSSE3 pixel-conversion functions,
  rather than raising the instruction-set baseline for the entire SDK.
The application uses BGRA SendImage without calling those conversion routines.

The upstream spout2-sys package declares BSD-2-Clause but omits its root license
file; LICENSE is preserved verbatim from the sibling spout2-rs 0.1.1 package
(same author and release), alongside the SDK own license.
